### `loadBoard(rows)`
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
### `loadBoard(state, rows)`
{{else}}
### `loadBoard(rows)`
{{/if}}

Poses an arbitrary board. `rows` is the board notation `specs/board.md` defines,
one string per row, `GRID_ROWS` (`8`) of them carrying `GRID_COLS` (`8`) tokens
each, and the board it writes takes those dimensions. Every gem of a posed board
is standing still where it was written, so every cell reports a `fell` of `0`.
Cell centers follow the formulas in `specs/board.md`, so a posed board sits on
the stage exactly where a dealt board does.

The board is the whole of what it writes: the screen, `menuIndex`, the phase and
its timers, the selection, the offer, the refusal, and every figure of the round
stand where they were.

A board posed this way is a board like any other, and the rules in
`specs/rules.md` govern it unchanged. Those rules run a chain from an accepted
swap and evaluate the level and end conditions when one settles, so a posed
board rests exactly as it was written until a swap is accepted on it.

