{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
### `requestSwap(colA, rowA, colB, rowB)`
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
### `requestSwap(state, colA, rowA, colB, rowB)`
{{else}}
### `requestSwap(colA, rowA, colB, rowB)`
{{/if}}

Requests the swap of `(colA, rowA)` with `(colB, rowB)` through the same
acceptance path a player's release takes, so R1, R2, and R3 in `specs/rules.md`
decide it and nothing is bypassed. An accepted swap exchanges the two cells and
puts the game into `swapping`, its first chain step resolving once
`SWAP_SECONDS` (`0.18`) of game time has passed, exactly as `specs/rules.md`
describes. A refused swap leaves the board as it stands and names the two cells
as the standing refusal for `REFUSAL_SECONDS` (`0.3`).

It names both cells itself, so the selection and the offer stand where they were
either way.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
### `pointerDown(x, y, device)`, `pointerMove(x, y, device)`, `pointerUp(device)`
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
### `pointerDown(state, x, y, device)`, `pointerMove(state, x, y, device)`, `pointerUp(state, device)`
{{else}}
### `pointerDown(x, y, device)`, `pointerMove(x, y, device)`, `pointerUp(device)`
{{/if}}

Report a press, a move, and a release at a logical stage position, from
`device`, which is `"mouse"`, `"pen"`, or `"touch"` and defaults to `"mouse"`.
The three drive the same input path a real pointer drives, so a posed touch and
a posed mouse differ only in the `device` the state reports, and a posed press
and a player's press are the same event to the game.

On the screens that carry pointer targets the three operate those targets by
exactly the rules in `specs/controls.md`: a move highlights, a press highlights
and arms, and a release inside the armed target takes it.

On `playing`, outside that screen's `pause` target, a press resolves against the
cell whose center is within `GEM_HIT_R` (`36`) of `(x, y)` by exactly the press
rules in `specs/controls.md`, a move offers the selected gem into an
orthogonally adjacent cell or withdraws the offer under those same rules, and
the release with an offer standing requests that swap, which R1, R2, and R3 in
`specs/rules.md` decide like any other.

Each of the three **takes effect immediately**, when it is called, rather than
{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
being sampled once per update. The press, the move, or the release is resolved
in the state the call returns rather than deferred to the next update. No frame
need pass between them, so a selection and the swap it leads to can both be
posed without advancing the game at all.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
being sampled once per update. The press, the move, or the release is resolved
in the state the call returns rather than deferred to the next update. Each
returns the state that press, move, or release left behind, and the next call is
handed that state, so a selection and the swap it leads to can both be posed
without a frame passing between the calls.
{{else}}
being sampled once per frame. The press, the move, or the release is resolved
against the live state before the call returns rather than deferred to the next
frame, through the same per-sample resolution the player controller feeds each
frame. No frame need pass between them, so a selection and the swap it leads to
can both be posed without advancing the game at all.
{{/if}}

A press on `playing` farther than `GEM_HIT_R` from every cell center and outside
every target leaves the board as it stands and clears the selection, as
`specs/controls.md` states.

