## Snapshot shape

`snapshot()` returns:
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
## Snapshot shape

`snapshot` returns:
{{else}}
## Snapshot shape

`snapshot()` returns:
{{/if}}

```js
{
  version: 1,
  screen: "title" | "howto" | "playing" | "paused" | "levelclear" | "gameover",
  menuIndex: <number>,        // the screen's highlighted menu item, from 0
  score: <number>,
  level: <number>,            // the level being played, counted from 1
  levelScore: <number>,       // banked toward the current level
  levelTarget: <number>,      // LEVEL_TARGET_STEP * level, derived
  phase: "idle" | "swapping" | "resolving",
  chainStep: <number>,        // 0 unless resolving
  multiplier: <number>,       // min(chainStep, MAX_MULTIPLIER), derived
  swapTimer: <number>,        // game time accumulated into the swap in motion
  stepTimer: <number>,        // game time accumulated into the step in progress
  stepHold: <number>,         // how long the step in progress holds, derived
  board: {
    cols: <number>,
    rows: <number>,
    cells: [
      { col, row, x, y,
        kind: <string | null>,
        cut: "plain" | "brilliant" | "star" | "prism",
        strain: <number>,
        fell: <number> },
    ],
  },
  selection: { col: <number>, row: <number> } | null,
  offer: { col: <number>, row: <number> } | null,
  refusal: { a: { col, row }, b: { col, row } } | null,
  lastCleared: <number>,      // cells cleared by the most recent chain step
  lastPoints: <number>,       // points the most recent chain step scored
  lastWaves: <number>,        // the greatest wave that step's clear set carried
  lastFall: <number>,         // the greatest fell on the board, derived
  moveScore: <number>,        // points the move currently running has scored
  bestMove: <number>,         // the level's best move
  bestChain: <number>,        // the level's deepest chain step
  legalSwap: <boolean>,       // whether any legal swap exists, derived
  refillKinds: [<string>, ...], // GRID_COLS entries, one per column
  pointer: { x: <number>, y: <number>, down: <boolean>,
             device: "mouse" | "pen" | "touch" },
  armedTarget: <string | null>,
  targets: [
    { id: <string>, x: <number>, y: <number>, w: <number>, h: <number> },
  ],
  muted: <boolean>,
  simTime: <number>,          // accumulated simulation time, in seconds
}
```

The shape is fixed, and every field is present on every screen. A field with
nothing to report holds its resting value rather than going missing: `board` is
`{ cols: 0, rows: 0, cells: [] }` while no board is in play, `selection`,
`offer`, `refusal` and `armedTarget` are `null` while none stands, `chainStep`
and `stepTimer` are `0` while `phase` is not `resolving`, `swapTimer` is `0`
while `phase` is not `swapping`, `refillKinds` holds `GRID_COLS` (`8`) entries
whatever the board, each the string `setRefillKinds` posed for that column and
`""` for a column that draws, and `menuIndex` is live on every screen
carrying a menu and rests at `0` on `playing`. `cells` lists every cell of the
board in reading order from the top-left cell to the bottom-right, and a cell's
`kind` is `null` for a `prism`.

`targets` lists the current screen's pointer targets, under the ids and in the
order `specs/controls.md` fixes for that screen, each with its top-left corner
and its size in the stage's logical units. A target's rectangle is the one the
game actually hit-tests against, so pressing and releasing at a listed target's
center takes that target.

Every field is read straight off the game's state, so what the snapshot reports
is what the game holds. Seven follow from other fields rather than being
reported independently:

| Field | Derived from |
| --- | --- |
| a cell's `x`, `y` | the cell center formulas in `specs/board.md` |
| `levelTarget` | `LEVEL_TARGET_STEP` (`2000`) times `level` |
| `multiplier` | `min(chainStep, MAX_MULTIPLIER)`, `MAX_MULTIPLIER` (`8`) |
| `lastFall` | the greatest `fell` on the board |
| `stepHold` | `lastWaves * WAVE_SECONDS + lastFall * FALL_SECONDS_PER_ROW + STEP_SECONDS`, as `specs/rules.md` fixes it |
| `legalSwap` | R1 and R3 in `specs/rules.md`, over the board as it stands |
| `targets` | the current screen's targets in `specs/controls.md` |

Three fields need the game to keep them honest every frame:

- `pointer` mirrors the position the pointer input reports, whether the pointer
  is currently pressed, and the device that drove it, refreshed in every update.
- `muted` mirrors the runtime's mute bit, refreshed in every update, since the
  runtime owns muting and this is the game's readable copy of it.
- `simTime` accumulates the delta time of every update, whatever the screen.

## Diagnostics

The runtime's debug overlay shows the values the game registers with it as
diagnostic sources. Register at least the current `screen` and `phase`, the
board's `cols` and `rows`, the score, the level and the level score against the
level's target, the chain step and the multiplier, how many cells the most
recent chain step cleared, what it scored, its `lastWaves` and its `lastFall`,
the selected cell and the offered cell, the level's best move and longest chain,
whether a legal swap exists, and the pointer position with the device that drove
it, the same facts the snapshot reports. Keep each one short enough to read on a
line, and keep every source a pure read, so watching the overlay leaves the game
as it is.

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
The overlay is part of the runtime layer you write. It draws the registered
sources, it is shown and hidden by the backtick key (`KeyboardEvent.code`
`Backquote`), and it reads the game without changing it.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
Registering those values is the whole of Facet's part, through
